WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.053
The Telephony module lets people on your team make and take phone calls from the browser.

00:00:06.053 --> 00:00:09.989
This video shows why it exists, how the phone system, the soft phone

00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:13.500
and the extensions fit together, and how to set up each one.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.423
Phone calls are still how many customers reach you.

00:00:21.423 --> 00:00:25.678
But a desk phone knows nothing about the customer on the other end,

00:00:25.678 --> 00:00:28.010
so every call starts from scratch.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.857
Phone companies also work in different ways.

00:00:31.857 --> 00:00:36.626
Moving from one to another, or running more than one, usually means new

00:00:36.626 --> 00:00:38.670
equipment and new training.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.740
Colleagues need to reach each other inside the company, without dialing a full

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.260
phone number or remembering who sits where.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:51.286
The Telephony module puts a phone in the browser, next to your site.

00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:55.910
You connect your phone company once, and every user places and takes calls

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.470
from the same screen.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.299
A provider is the phone system that carries your calls.

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:09.581
The site works with Telnyx, a phone service in the cloud, and with

00:01:09.581 --> 00:01:13.210
Asterisk, a phone system that your company runs itself.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.220
The default provider is the one the soft phone uses.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.840
You can connect more than one provider, and switch the default without changing anything else.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.184
The soft phone is the phone itself, in the browser.

00:01:27.184 --> 00:01:31.030
It has a keypad, a list of recent calls, and voicemail.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.457
An extension is a short internal number that belongs to one user, so

00:01:36.457 --> 00:01:41.070
colleagues can call or transfer to each other by number or by name.

00:01:45.257 --> 00:01:48.482
Open Tools, Features, and search for Telephony.

00:01:48.482 --> 00:01:50.917
The Telephony feature is the base:

00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:57.187
it adds the settings, the extensions and the connection between the browser and the phone system.

00:01:57.641 --> 00:02:00.142
The soft phone has its own features.

00:02:00.142 --> 00:02:04.431
One puts a phone button on every admin page, and another opens the

00:02:04.431 --> 00:02:08.421
phone in a small window of its own, which the phone apps use.

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:11.627
Each phone system is a feature too.

00:02:11.627 --> 00:02:16.327
Turn on Telnyx, Asterisk, or both, and each one adds its own tab

00:02:16.327 --> 00:02:18.475
to the Telephony settings.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.351
By default, call recordings are stored on your site, encrypted.

00:02:23.351 --> 00:02:28.541
A feature called Telephony, Azure Blob Storage moves them to Azure instead.

00:02:28.541 --> 00:02:32.130
Your technical team turns it on and configures it.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:41.133
Open Settings, Communication, Telephony, and choose the Asterisk tab.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:45.764
Use Asterisk when your company runs its own Asterisk phone system.

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.980
The values come from whoever looks after it.

00:02:49.432 --> 00:02:51.507
Tick Enable Asterisk provider.

00:02:51.507 --> 00:02:53.582
The rest of the fields appear.

00:02:54.035 --> 00:02:59.287
Enter the ARI base URL, the ARI user name and the ARI password.

00:02:59.287 --> 00:03:04.235
The password is stored encrypted, and is never shown again.

00:03:04.685 --> 00:03:07.524
The Stasis application name is required.

00:03:07.524 --> 00:03:12.524
When several sites share one Asterisk server, each site needs its own name,

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:15.795
so that sites never receive each other's calls.

00:03:16.249 --> 00:03:21.465
The optional fields set an Endpoint template, an Outbound caller id, the Dial

00:03:21.465 --> 00:03:23.979
timeout and the voicemail details.

00:03:23.979 --> 00:03:28.629
The browser audio fields below them carry call audio to the browser.

00:03:29.082 --> 00:03:30.061
Click Save.

00:03:30.061 --> 00:03:34.265
The site checks the required fields, but it does not call the phone

00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:38.872
system, so a wrong password shows up the first time someone places a call.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.906
Choose the Telnyx tab.

00:03:44.906 --> 00:03:47.544
A blue panel lists the four steps.

00:03:47.544 --> 00:03:52.490
Before you start, create an API key, version 2, in the Telnyx portal.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:56.776
Sign in as an account owner or admin, so the key can create

00:03:56.776 --> 00:03:58.490
what the site needs.

00:03:58.946 --> 00:04:04.364
Tick Enable Telnyx provider, paste the key into API key, and click Save.

00:04:04.364 --> 00:04:06.726
The key is stored encrypted.

00:04:07.485 --> 00:04:11.291
Once the key is stored, a Connect Telnyx button appears.

00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:16.755
Clicking it creates the call application, the connection and the voice profile that

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:20.685
Telnyx needs, and shows a green Connected to Telnyx panel.

00:04:22.285 --> 00:04:27.025
After you connect, the page also asks for the Default outbound caller id,

00:04:27.025 --> 00:04:31.945
the number your customers see, and the Webhook public key, which proves that

00:04:31.945 --> 00:04:34.465
call events really come from Telnyx.

00:04:34.465 --> 00:04:37.165
Without that key, calls do not connect.

00:04:37.915 --> 00:04:42.907
It also offers Noise suppression, which cleans background sound out of calls, and

00:04:42.907 --> 00:04:46.464
an Advanced section for rarely changed network settings.

00:04:46.464 --> 00:04:48.645
Every one has a working default.

00:04:52.829 --> 00:04:58.483
On the Soft Phone tab, the Default telephony provider lists every provider you turned on.

00:04:58.483 --> 00:05:02.529
The soft phone places and controls its calls through this one.

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:07.554
Allowed short codes lists short numbers people may dial, one per line, such

00:05:07.554 --> 00:05:09.472
as a carrier service number.

00:05:09.472 --> 00:05:12.576
Short numbers are refused unless they are listed.

00:05:12.576 --> 00:05:15.003
Emergency numbers can never be added.

00:05:15.457 --> 00:05:19.514
Enable the soft phone is a master switch for the whole site.

00:05:19.514 --> 00:05:25.107
Show the soft phone on the admin dashboard puts the phone button on every admin page.

00:05:25.559 --> 00:05:31.374
Enable the diagnostics tab adds a tab with live call quality and a microphone meter.

00:05:31.374 --> 00:05:34.539
Turn it on to troubleshoot, then off again.

00:05:34.992 --> 00:05:39.151
Recent calls to display sets how many calls the Recent tab lists.

00:05:39.151 --> 00:05:44.364
Default country decides the country a national number starts with, and Accent color

00:05:44.364 --> 00:05:46.942
sets the color of the phone's buttons.

00:05:47.396 --> 00:05:48.468
Click Save.

00:05:48.468 --> 00:05:51.306
The phone now uses the chosen provider.

00:05:55.506 --> 00:05:59.299
Open Interaction Center, Management, Extensions.

00:05:59.299 --> 00:06:02.249
The list is empty until you add one.

00:06:02.249 --> 00:06:04.076
Click Add extension.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:09.053
Display name is what a colleague sees when this extension calls them.

00:06:09.053 --> 00:06:11.640
Leave it empty to show the user name.

00:06:12.093 --> 00:06:16.864
Extension number is the number colleagues dial, such as 1001.

00:06:16.864 --> 00:06:18.573
It must be unique.

00:06:19.026 --> 00:06:22.013
User is the person the extension rings.

00:06:22.013 --> 00:06:26.326
Type to search the enabled users, pick one, and click Save.

00:06:26.777 --> 00:06:29.984
Add an extension for each person who takes calls.

00:06:29.984 --> 00:06:34.240
The list shows each number, its display name and the user it rings,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.097
and you can search it by number or by name.

00:06:37.548 --> 00:06:40.939
Every saved extension can be dialed straight away.

00:06:40.939 --> 00:06:44.028
To stop one ringing, delete it from the list.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:52.940
The phone button at the bottom right of every admin page opens the soft phone.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.926
The status in its header says what it is doing.

00:06:55.926 --> 00:06:58.067
Ready means it can place a call.

00:06:58.519 --> 00:07:02.288
On the Keypad tab, type a phone number or use the keys.

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:07.849
The flag sets the country, so a national number becomes a full international number.

00:07:07.849 --> 00:07:10.259
The green button places the call.

00:07:10.715 --> 00:07:13.681
Click Dial extension to call a colleague.

00:07:13.681 --> 00:07:19.045
Type the extension number, or part of a name, and the phone shows who it rings.

00:07:19.495 --> 00:07:23.666
The Recent tab lists incoming, outgoing and missed calls.

00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:25.785
Click one to dial it back.

00:07:26.235 --> 00:07:30.171
The Voicemail tab lists the messages left for you, with a badge that

00:07:30.171 --> 00:07:32.405
counts the ones you have not played.

00:07:32.855 --> 00:07:36.707
Agents usually run the phone in a window of its own, through the

00:07:36.707 --> 00:07:39.072
browser extension or the Windows app.

00:07:39.072 --> 00:07:42.594
It opens the soft phone page of your site, so a call keeps

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:47.545
going while you move around, and incoming calls ring even when the window is closed.

00:07:51.733 --> 00:07:55.036
Open Access Control, Roles and edit a role.

00:07:55.036 --> 00:07:57.936
Type Telephony in Search permissions:

00:07:57.936 --> 00:08:00.633
the module adds three permissions.

00:08:01.084 --> 00:08:04.845
Manage telephony settings opens the Telephony settings.

00:08:04.845 --> 00:08:08.544
Manage telephony extensions opens the extensions list.

00:08:08.997 --> 00:08:13.093
Use the telephony soft phone lets a person make and take calls.

00:08:13.093 --> 00:08:17.308
Only the Administrator role has it by default, so add it to every

00:08:17.308 --> 00:08:19.267
role that works the phones.

00:08:23.467 --> 00:08:28.051
A small team without desk phones gives each person a browser phone, and

00:08:28.051 --> 00:08:31.267
an extension so colleagues reach them by number.

00:08:32.017 --> 00:08:36.251
A company with its own Asterisk server keeps it, and gives its staff

00:08:36.251 --> 00:08:39.627
a phone in the browser, next to the customer records.

00:08:40.377 --> 00:08:45.403
A business that outgrows one phone company connects a second provider, and changes

00:08:45.403 --> 00:08:48.317
the default provider when it is time to move.

00:08:49.067 --> 00:08:53.925
A support or sales team that needs queues, campaigns and a dashboard adds

00:08:53.925 --> 00:08:57.247
the Contact Center on top of the same telephony.

00:08:59.247 --> 00:09:04.550
Connect your phone system once, choose the default provider, give people extensions, and

00:09:04.550 --> 00:09:07.879
every user can place and take calls from the browser.

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:09.347
Thanks for watching.

